content.summary:
The sprint met its goal on macOS. One click on New chat opens a terminal in the app's main window. The terminal runs in the folder's canonical path and runs the folder's agent CLI, with a per-chat `dm` grant (verified live with Claude Code and in the packaged arm64 app).

Chats are terminals end to end:
- switching chats and reloading keep the process and restore the screen;
- Start again resumes Claude sessions, including chats created before the change;
- quiet terminals are idle-stopped;
- sign-in runs in a terminal in the window;
- Start run opens an orchestrator terminal that receives its kickoff;
- quitting leaves no process behind.

The protocol adapters, approval and streaming code and the Claude Agent SDK are gone. Custom CLIs no longer have a protocol, and existing ACP and Codex rows are migrated to a review state. All 16 required tickets and the acceptance node are accepted.

The Definition of Done passed. The first coverage run failed (functions 95.54%, branches 94.42%) and was fixed with tests only. Fireguard graded the sprint A/94 and the added tests A/100. The optional Windows ticket DM-333 did not run, because this Mac host cannot meet its windows environment.
